{"`klog.NewContext` is called with `d.Log` (base logger) instead of the enriched `log` variable. This means the context passed to downstream calls loses the `name`, `kind`, and `method` log fields that every other method correctly attaches.": 0.9916348457336426, "Storage failure path calls `d.recordLegacyDuration` instead of `d.recordStorageDuration`, recording the failed storage operation under the wrong metric.": 0.9949595928192139, "`name` (the object name) is passed as the resource-kind argument to `recordStorageDuration`. Every other call in this file passes `options.Kind`. This will create a separate metric time-series per object name, causing unbounded cardinality.": 0.9781364798545837, "The legacy `DeleteCollection` operation in the goroutine calls `d.recordStorageDuration` instead of `d.recordLegacyDuration`. This records legacy timing under the storage metric, corrupting both.": 0.9986101388931274, "The error test case sets up `setupLegacyFn` but leaves `setupStorageFn` nil. Since Mode 3 calls `Storage.Create` first, this should be `setupStorageFn`. It only works because both mocks share the same `*mock.Mock` instance.": 0.9081477522850037}